Spec clarifications for datagate, second batch: the two sentences behind the v8B-disambiguated
run's misses (2 of 405, 2026-09-03; notes/v8B-disambiguated-misses.md, judge run
outputs/judge/v8B-four). Both are worded to match the hidden tests and the reference
solution (`_parse_bool` strips then rejects anything outside the eight tokens;
`query.get("enrich", []) == ["yes"]` enriches only on a single occurrence).

These are not the same kind of miss as the first five. On T72 the blind judges read the
sentence the tests' way 20 of 20 and only the tester read it the other way; on T104 the
tester declared the mixed repetition unresolved and asserted nothing, and the
implementation fell through to a library default. The prompt-side fix for the second is
configs/prompts/v8-choice-must-decide.patch. NOT APPLIED to any run as of 2026-09-03.

  checkpoint_6  T72/T73  a boolean value empty after trimming is invalid
  checkpoint_7  T104     a repeated `enrich` parameter keeps enrichment off

Applies on top of datagate-clarified.patch:

  bin/spec-patch datagate                                 # rebuilds problems/datagate with the first patch
  patch -p1 -d problems < problems/datagate-clarified-2.patch

